  "planning_notes": [
    "Board is Arduino Uno; D0/D1 reserved for Serial RX/TX by rule; no other serial pins are assumed.",
    "The exact proximity sensor electrical level (active-high/active-low) and pullup need are not specified; default digital_input initial=false is used and active level handling is assumed to be modeled in SysML based on observed wiring (no active_high/pullup override provided).",
    "Ultrasonic distance/validity share the same trigger_pin/echo_pin (D8/D9) and use HC-SR04 assumptions with acquisition bundled per acquisition frame; invalid/out-of-range retains last distance and sets validity false.",
    "TM1637 displays remaining water percentage and today's usage count; a single tm1637_number port is provided and the switching/formatting behavior is assumed to be implemented in SysML (no multiplexing or extra GPIO for TM1637 buses).",
    "Water valve ON duration, low-level threshold logic, and today's usage counter/timestamping are modeled in SysML using real elapsed_ms; device requests carry only hardware I/O.",
    "Serial query trigger/command decoding is required by the prose but not specified in the provided requirements as concrete command tokens; therefore only an on-demand report gate is defined, and command parsing is assumed to be implemented in SysML (no serial_command_input request was added because command tokens are not given)."
  ],
